this process. Metagenomic, PCR-DGGE and faecal short chain fatty acids analyses were performed on faecal samples obtained from three infants before and after the administration of each dose of vaccine. We found a high inter-individual variability in the early lifegut microbiota at microbial composition level, but a large similarity between the infants’ microbiomes at functional level. Rotavirus vaccination did not show any major effects upon the infant gut microbiota. Thus, the individual microbiome establishment and development process seems to occur in a defined manner during the first stages of life and it is not affected by oral rotavirus vaccination.","trial_population_condition":"healthy_control","urls":{"ena":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ena/browser/view/PRJEB6972","evidence_csv_gz":"https://olmlab.github.io/microbiome_repo/data/studies/PRJEB6972_determinations.csv.gz","page":"https://olmlab.github.io/microbiome_repo/studies/PRJEB6972.html","samples_csv":"https://olmlab.github.io/microbiome_repo/api/samples/PRJEB6972.csv","samples_full_csv_gz":"https://olmlab.github.io/microbiome_repo/data/studies/PRJEB6972.csv.gz"}},{"accession":"PRJNA1067375","age_categories":{"unknown":11},"countries":{"KR":11},"first_public_year":"2024","gbp_per_sample_median":6.79,"has_cases_and_healthy_controls":false,"has_treated_and_control_arms":false,"health_conditions":{"healthy_control":11},"intervention_design":"observational_with_procedure","intervention_detail":"SARS-CoV-2 vaccination (primary series and booster)","interventions":["vaccine"],"n_samples":11,"papers":[{"doi":"10.1186/s12967-024-05637-2","pmcid":"PMC11380214","pmid":"39242525","title":"The gut microbiota modifies antibody durability and booster responses after SARS-CoV-2 vaccination."}],"sample_intervention_arms":{},"sex":{},"title":"Gut microbiome after SARS-CoV-2 vaccination","trial_population_condition":"healthy_control","urls":{"ena":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ena/browser/view/PRJNA1067375","evidence_csv_gz":"https://ol